17:["$","main",null,{"id":"top","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"border-b border-ink/10 bg-surface/40","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 py-10 sm:px-8","children":[["$","$Ld",null,{"href":"/operating-system","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm font-semibold text-mute transition hover:text-accent","children":"← All chapters"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-5 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-accent","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"rounded-full bg-accent/12 px-2.5 py-0.5","children":"Chapter 36"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-mute","children":["· ",18," min read · illustrated"]}]]}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"mt-3 font-hand text-5xl font-bold leading-tight text-ink sm:text-6xl","children":"OS for Engineers: Performance & Debugging"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-lg text-mute","children":"A methodical way to find which of the four resources is choking your system, and the exact tool that proves it"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-6 flex max-w-2xl flex-col gap-3","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-[1.02rem] leading-[1.75] text-ink/85","children":"You have shipped the service. It passed every test on your laptop. Then at 2 a.m. the pager goes off: latency is up, the box is \"slow\", and someone in the incident channel types the most useless sentence in engineering: \"it might be a memory leak?\". This chapter is about never having to guess again. Everything the earlier chapters taught you, the run queue, context switches, page faults, the page cache, I/O wait, swap, was building toward this moment, because a production performance problem is just an operating-system concept wearing a business costume."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"text-[1.02rem] leading-[1.75] text-ink/85","children":"The core insight is small and freeing: a machine has exactly four physical resources: CPU, memory, disk I/O, and network, and every slowdown, without exception, is one of them running out of room. Your job during an incident is not to read the whole codebase. It is to walk the four resources in order, ask two questions of each (\"how busy is it?\" and \"is anything queuing or failing?\"), and let the numbers point at the bottleneck. That discipline has a name, the USE method, and it turns firefighting into a checklist."}],["$","p","2",{"className":"text-[1.02rem] leading-[1.75] text-ink/85","children":"This is the chapter engineers bookmark, so it is deliberately dense with real commands and real output. We will read load average against core count, decode every column of top, tell a genuinely full memory apart from a healthy page cache, catch a disk that is saturated versus one that is merely slow, watch context switches spike under lock contention, and finally trace and profile a live process with strace, perf, and flame graphs. We close with a symptom-to-tool-to-cause playbook you can run cold at 2 a.m., and a handoff to the database capstone, where all of this lands on one real system."}]]}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto flex max-w-6xl gap-10 px-5 py-12 sm:px-8","children":[["$","nav",null,{"className":"sticky top-8 hidden h-fit w-56 shrink-0 lg:block","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-3 font-hand text-xl font-bold text-ink","children":"On this page"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-1.5 text-sm","children":[["$","li","01-four-resources",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#01-four-resources","className":"flex gap-2 rounded-md px-2 py-1 text-mute transition hover:bg-accent/10 hover:text-accent","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent/70","children":"01"}],"$L21"]}]}],"$L22","$L23","$L24","$L25","$L26","$L27","$L28"]}]]}],"$L29"]}],"$L2a"]}]
